## Native libraries

### Poppler (GPL-2.0-or-later)

The Flatpak bundle contains Poppler 26.11.0 (libpoppler and libpoppler-glib),
© The Poppler developers, built from
<https://poppler.freedesktop.org/poppler-26.11.0.tar.xz>. Poppler is licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later; parts derived from
Xpdf are under "GPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0". Pygoscribe uses it under GPL-3.0. The
exact source tarball is attached to each Pygoscribe release next to the
.flatpak. The full text of the GPL-3.0 is in `LICENSE`; the GPL-2.0 is at
<https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html>. The .deb uses the
distribution's own Poppler package instead.

### GTK, libadwaita, GLib, Pango, gdk-pixbuf, graphene, Cairo

Linked dynamically from the system (.deb) or the GNOME runtime (Flatpak);
not shipped with Pygoscribe. They are licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later
(Cairo: LGPL-2.1 or MPL-1.1).

